  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="meta">Effective date: 1 January 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Version 1.0</p>
</header>

<p>
  Durar Jewelry Museum ("Durar", "we", "us") respects your privacy. This policy explains
  what information the Durar mobile application collects, how it is used, and the choices
  you have over it.
</p>

<div class="note">
  <strong>In short:</strong> we collect only what is needed to run the app — your account
  details, your orders and bookings, and your bids. We do not sell your personal
  information, and you can delete your account and all associated data at any time.
</div>

<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

<h3>1.1 Information you provide directly</h3>
<p>When you create an account or interact with the app, you may provide:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account details</strong> — full name, email address, phone number, and password.</li>
  <li><strong>Profile photo</strong> — optional avatar image you choose to upload.</li>
  <li><strong>Delivery details</strong> — city and shipping address, required only when you place an order.</li>
  <li><strong>Review content</strong> — a star rating and written comment when you review a product.</li>
  <li><strong>Museum booking details</strong> — your name, national ID number, and phone number when you reserve a museum ticket.</li>
</ul>

<h3>1.2 Information collected automatically</h3>
<p>To keep the app working correctly and to protect against abuse, we also record:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Device identifier</strong> — a randomly generated ID created on your device and sent with each request. It is used to recognise guest sessions and to prevent fraudulent bidding or duplicate ticket reservations. It is not tied to your hardware identifier.</li>
  <li><strong>App language preference</strong> — your Arabic/English selection.</li>
  <li><strong>Wishlist and cart contents</strong> — stored so your saved pieces and basket persist between sessions.</li>
  <li><strong>Push notification token</strong> — used to deliver alerts about your orders, auctions, and bookings.</li>
</ul>

<h3>1.3 What we do NOT collect</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Payment card numbers, CVV, or bank credentials — payments are processed entirely by a third-party payment gateway; we never see or store your card data.</li>
  <li>Precise location or contacts.</li>
  <li>Data from children under 13 — we do not knowingly collect it.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
<p>We use your data solely to operate the service:</p>
<ul>
  <li>To create, authenticate, and manage your account.</li>
  <li>To process orders, apply discount coupons, and arrange delivery.</li>
  <li>To run live auctions, record your bids, and notify you if you win.</li>
  <li>To reserve museum tickets and validate them at the entrance.</li>
  <li>To publish reviews you choose to submit.</li>
  <li>To send notifications about your account, orders, and bookings.</li>
  <li>To detect, prevent, and investigate fraud or abuse.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Legal Bases for Processing (GDPR)</h2>
<p>Where the GDPR applies, we process personal data under the following bases:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Account creation and authentication</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Order processing and delivery</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Auctions and museum bookings</td><td>Performance of a contract</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Notifications about your account</td><td>Legitimate interests</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Fraud prevention and security</td><td>Legitimate interests</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Marketing communications</td><td>Consent (withdrawable at any time)</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>4. Data Sharing</h2>
<p>We do not sell your personal information. We share data only with the parties strictly necessary to fulfil your request:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Payment gateway</strong> — to process transactions.</li>
  <li><strong>Courier / shipping providers</strong> — to deliver your order.</li>
  <li><strong>Push notification service</strong> — to deliver app notifications.</li>
  <li><strong>Cloud infrastructure and error-reporting providers</strong> — under data-processing agreements, for hosting and reliability.</li>
  <li><strong>Law enforcement or regulators</strong> — where disclosure is legally required.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Each recipient receives only the data it needs to perform its part, and none of these
  parties may use your data for its own purposes.
</p>

<h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
<p>We keep your data only for as long as necessary:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account data</strong> — for as long as your account is active.</li>
  <li><strong>Order and booking records</strong> — retained as required by applicable tax and commercial law.</li>
  <li><strong>Device identifier</strong> — cleared when you sign out.</li>
  <li><strong>Reviews</strong> — remain public unless you request removal.</li>
</ul>

<h2>6. Security</h2>
<p>
  All data is transmitted over encrypted HTTPS connections. Authentication tokens and the
  device identifier are stored in the operating system's secure, app-sandboxed storage and
  are never exposed to other applications on your device.
</p>
<p>
  No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, but we apply reasonable
  technical and organisational measures to protect your data against unauthorised access,
  alteration, or disclosure.
</p>

<h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
<p>Subject to your local law, you have the right to:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
  <li><strong>Correct</strong> — update or fix inaccurate data from your profile.</li>
  <li><strong>Delete</strong> — permanently delete your account and all associated data, from <em>Profile → Security → Delete Your Account</em>.</li>
  <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> — stop receiving marketing messages at any time.</li>
  <li><strong>Object and complain</strong> — contact us, and lodge a complaint with your local data-protection authority.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
<p>
  Durar is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
  data from them. If you believe a child has provided us with data, please contact us and
  we will delete it promptly.
</p>

<h2>9. International Transfers</h2>
<p>
  Durar is operated from Saudi Arabia. If your data is processed outside your country of
  residence, we rely on recognised transfer safeguards such as Standard Contractual
  Clauses where applicable.
</p>

<h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>
  We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be announced within
  the app or on this page, and the "Effective date" above will be revised.
</p>

